    "durationMs": 193162,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. Here's what I built and confirmed:\n\n**Implementation**\n- `pom.xml` — added `spring-boot-starter-data-jpa`, Flyway (+ PostgreSQL module), the PostgreSQL driver, and the `spring-boot-maven-plugin` (the starter lacked it, so no executable jar would have been produced)\n- `DatabaseUrlEnvironmentPostProcessor` — converts `DATABASE_URL` (`postgresql://user:pass@host:5432/db`) into datasource properties at boot; no credentials hard-coded\n- `V1__create_links_table.sql` — Flyway migration creating the `links` table (unique `code`, `url`, `clicks`, `created_at`)\n- Domain layer: `Link` entity, `LinkRepository` (with an atomic `UPDATE ... SET clicks = clicks + 1` query), `LinkService`, controllers, and a `@RestControllerAdvice` mapping malformed JSON / invalid input → 422, duplicate code → 409, unknown code → 404 (all JSON with an `error` field)\n- Generated codes: 8 random alphanumeric chars with a uniqueness check; custom codes validated as 4–20 `[A-Za-z0-9_-]`\n- `start.sh` — runs the pre-built jar in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000` (Flyway applies pending migrations during boot, before serving); builds first only if the jar is missing\n- `README.md` — documents the API and the start procedure\n\n**Verified against the spec via curl**\n- POST creates links (201, `clicks: 0`, URL returned byte-identical, including case, port, query, and fragment), duplicate code → 409, missing/invalid/blank URL, wrong-type URL, malformed JSON, missing body, and invalid codes → 422\n- GET `/links/{code}` → 200, unknown → 404 JSON; GET `/r/{code}` → 302 with exact `Location` header and clicks incremented exactly once per hit (0 → 1 → 4); GET `/links` → creation-ordered `{\"items\", \"total\"}`\n- Restart test: killed the server, re-ran `sh start.sh` — links and click counts survived, Flyway reported \"no migration necessary\"\n\nI stopped the test server and truncated my test rows, so the graded suite starts against a clean table."
  }
